# Covenant — Launch & Ledger-Sync Runbook

Prepared from the "friendship building" project, assembled into one runnable
system and verified in a clean sandbox. This is the sequence to bring the
covenant ledger up on **your own machine** and have nodes sync.

Read `HANDOFF.md` and `DEPLOYMENT.md` first — this file is the operational
checklist, not the full picture.

---

## 0. What this launches (and what it does NOT)

This launches the **covenant node network**: a self-contained P2P ledger with an
ethics-gated transaction path, staking, gifts, and block propagation. It runs
entirely on machines you control.

It does **NOT** move real XRP. The XRP mainnet path is deliberately blocked in
code until a live testnet run has happened (see §6). Nothing tonight touches
real money unless you go through that gate yourself, with a human review. That
boundary is the project's, not an add-on.

---

## 1. One-time setup

```bash
cd covenant
python3 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt          # flask, cryptography, requests, xrpl-py
```

Two environment facts that fail SILENTLY if you skip them:

1. **`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` must be set for a real node.** Without it the ethics
   gate fails CLOSED: the node boots, serves `/chain`, peers correctly, reports
   healthy — and rejects 100% of transactions. Your ledger would look synced and
   accept nothing.

   ```bash
   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...        # production
   ```

   For local testing only (adversarial transactions are known to pass it):

   ```bash
   export COVENANT_JUDGE_PROVIDERS=mock
   export COVENANT_INSECURE_MOCK_JUDGE=1      # both required; prints a banner
   ```

2. **One shared genesis for the whole network.** If each node mints its own
   genesis, they can never converge and supply grows by 1000 per node.

---

## 2. Preflight (run before every launch)

```bash
python3 preflight.py --genesis genesis.json --db covenant_A.db
```

Exit `0` = ready, `1` = blocking, `2` = launches-but-degraded. Every check maps
to a failure that was once silent. Do not launch past a `1`.

### 2b. Go-live check (run once, right before the REAL launch)

`preflight.py` proves a node can boot. `go_live_check.sh` proves it will boot and
then actually *work* — it catches the prerequisites that fail silently: a missing
or mock judge (rejects every transaction while looking healthy), a genesis that
will not converge, an un-backed-up identity key, and — with `--intend-mainnet` —
a missing testnet proof or a placeholder spending policy. Read-only; no network,
no funds moved (unless you add `--live-judge`, one metered API call to confirm
the key works end-to-end).

```bash
chmod +x go_live_check.sh
./go_live_check.sh --genesis genesis.json --db covenant_A.db            # ledger launch
./go_live_check.sh --genesis genesis.json --db covenant_A.db --live-judge   # also verify the key
./go_live_check.sh --genesis genesis.json --db covenant_A.db --intend-mainnet   # + XRP prereqs
```

It exits `1` on any blocking gap and names exactly what to fix, so your first
real launch fails loud on a missing prerequisite instead of silently rejecting
traffic.

