## 3. Mint the shared genesis (founder does this ONCE)

```bash
python3 covenant_unified_v8.py --export-genesis genesis.json
```

Distribute `genesis.json` to every node. It is signed by the founder's key and
re-verified on load (hash, proof-of-work, signature). **Back up
`covenant_A.db.key`** — it is the node's operator credential *and* the genesis
mint key. Lose it and the genesis balance is stranded forever.

---

## 4. Bring up the network

Each node binds three ports: `--port` (HTTP), `--port+1` (P2P), `--port+11`
(bridge). Space nodes ≥20 apart.

### A small full mesh (conservative default)

With finding AV fixed, a line/tree topology now propagates correctly by push, so
a mesh is no longer required — but it is still a clean, simple default for a
small launch, with every node one hop from any miner:

```bash
# Node A (founder — holds the genesis 1000)
python3 covenant_unified_v8.py --real --port 5000 --node-id A \
  --genesis genesis.json --peers 127.0.0.1:5021,127.0.0.1:5041

# Node B
python3 covenant_unified_v8.py --real --port 5020 --node-id B \
  --genesis genesis.json --peers 127.0.0.1:5001,127.0.0.1:5041

# Node C
python3 covenant_unified_v8.py --real --port 5040 --node-id C \
  --genesis genesis.json --peers 127.0.0.1:5001,127.0.0.1:5021
```

(`--peers` lists each other node's **P2P** port, i.e. its `--port + 1`.)

Verify:

```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:5000/chain   | head        # height 1 at genesis
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:5000/health              # single status signal
```

Point a monitor at `/health` — it returns `degraded` plus a `warnings` list
naming exactly what is wrong.

---

## 5. Confirm sync

Submit a signed transaction and mine on A (both are operator-authenticated;
`/mine` is rate-limited to 1 per 60s by design), then confirm every node's tip
hash matches:

```bash
for p in 5000 5020 5040; do
  curl -s http://127.0.0.1:$p/chain | python3 -c \
   "import sys,json;c=json.load(sys.stdin);c=c.get('chain',c);print('height',len(c),'tip',c[-1]['hash'][:12])"
done
```

All three heights and tips should agree. A late node started knowing only one
peer will catch up the whole chain on its own (verified).

