## 7. Propagation — finding AV, now FIXED

An earlier state of this bundle had `test_multinode_live.py` at a deterministic
**19/21**: a freshly-mined block reached a direct peer but not a node two hops
away in real time — it converged only via the periodic bootstrap pull.

Root cause (traced with a 3-process line A–B–C): the block was landing via the
bootstrap / gap-fill path, which **did not re-announce it onward**, so whenever
that pull path won its race against the announce/fetch push, the block reached a
node and stopped. **Fixed** in `covenant_unified_v8.py` (`_apply_fetched_blocks`
now re-announces every block it applies, like the other accept paths already do).

After the fix: **21/21 across four consecutive runs**, with the 2-hop node
reaching the new height in ~2s by push, and a full adversarial regression showing
no regression. So a line/tree topology now propagates correctly by push.

The full-mesh guidance in §4 is still a fine, conservative default for a small
launch, but it is no longer *required* to get non-adjacent nodes updated
promptly. See `SESSION_FINDINGS.md` finding AV for the full trace and the
adversarial-pass results.

